From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bpereira <bpereira@cloudflare.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 20:57:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 8/9] Compact retained Parley layouts

A retained paragraph layout kept growth slack and data most layouts
never use:

- Style metrics, inline boxes and other buffers drop their growth slack
  once a layout is built; mostly empty buffers are thin vectors.
- Laid-out underline and strikethrough decorations are boxed, since few
  runs have them.
- Shaped clusters store only the start of their characters, and
  cluster positions, styles, character ranges and grapheme starts are
  read through the shaped text instead of being copied per cluster.
- A build reuses the last resolved font family instead of resolving it
  again for every run with the same family.

Layout and paint output are unchanged.

Signed-off-by: bpereira <bpereira@cloudflare.com>
